{% comment %}
  Size chart modal, rendered from within blocks/variant-picker.liquid.
  Uses this theme's native <dialog scroll-lock> convention
  (assets/critical.css already handles body-scroll-lock and the base
  dialog color tokens globally via the
  html:has(dialog[scroll-lock][open]) rule) rather than a hand-rolled
  focus trap — <dialog> gives us focus containment and Escape-to-close
  natively via showModal().

  This is the first live use of that convention: the critical.css hook
  was pre-wired in an earlier task, but no section/block had actually
  rendered a <dialog scroll-lock> element until this snippet.

  The open/close JS deliberately does not live in this file's own
  javascript block. A prior task believed the javascript tag was safe
  in snippets (the stylesheet tag above genuinely is — see
  snippets/image.liquid), but live verification (the first real
  browser session available after a long static-only stretch) found
  that shopify theme dev's local asset bundler does not correctly
  extract a snippet's javascript-tag content: the generated bundle for
  this exact file included the file's other raw text ahead of the
  actual function body, producing a syntax error that silently broke
  the trigger for every visitor (confirmed by contrast: the equivalent
  bundling for blocks/gift-card-recipient.liquid extracts correctly —
  this is specifically a snippet-bundling gap, not a general theme-dev
  limitation). Whether Shopify's production CDN bundler handles this
  correctly is unconfirmed and beside the point: theme-dev is itself a
  real environment merchants and Theme Store reviewers preview
  through, so relying on behavior that's broken there isn't
  acceptable regardless of production behavior. The open/close logic
  now lives in assets/product-variant-picker.js (initSizeChartModal)
  instead — already proven working, and this snippet is only ever
  rendered from blocks/variant-picker.liquid, which only exists on the
  product template where that script is already loaded.

  size_chart_placeholder is deliberately placeholder copy — this
  environment has no real sizing-chart content/data (same category of
  gap as missing product photography elsewhere in this project).
{% endcomment %}

<button type="button" class="size-chart-trigger" data-size-chart-trigger>
  {{ 'product.size_chart' | t }}
</button>

<dialog class="size-chart-modal" scroll-lock data-size-chart-modal aria-label="{{ 'product.size_chart' | t }}">
  <button type="button" class="size-chart-modal__close" data-size-chart-close aria-label="{{ 'product.close' | t }}">&times;</button>
  <div class="size-chart-modal__content">
    {{ 'product.size_chart_placeholder' | t }}
  </div>
</dialog>

{% stylesheet %}
  .size-chart-trigger {
    align-self: flex-start;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    text-decoration: underline;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    min-height: 24px;
  }
  .size-chart-modal {
    max-width: 32rem;
    width: calc(100% - var(--space-6));
    border: none;
    padding: var(--space-6);
  }
  .size-chart-modal::backdrop {
    background: rgb(0 0 0 / 50%);
  }
  .size-chart-modal__close {
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--space-3);
    right: var(--space-3);
    min-width: 24px;
    min-height: 24px;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
